 me  into the the words and how they're used  but of course i've also been working  around the house these last couple of  days  there's been an amateur golf tournament  the canadian amateur golf tournament at  our golf club so i haven't been able to  play any golf so i have more time to  either work around the house or study  and of course all the time working  around the house i'm listening so i'm  listening to the same material the  iranian or the yeah the revolution so  i'm actually learning  about the  islamic revolution and the different  factions and the pati bourgeoisie or the  land owners or the labor group or the  the muslim extremists or the leftists  and all the different factions and  groups and how they  participated in or contributed to  the revolution of 1979.  part of the confusion i'm also getting  used to the iranian years i figured out  it's 621 years  less than our western calendar so you  get used to that  so a certain amount of focus here has  enabled me to pick up a number of  political terms  get a little more familiar with the  years that the iranians use the month is  still a bit of a  stretch for me  um  and and i get this  i feel that this degree of focus and  concentration has elevated my persian in  a way  uh that it wouldn't it wouldn't have  been possible without this degree of  concentration and focus now tomorrow i  will have my lesson with my tutor and we  will talk about  these events and we'll see how i do  my hope is that my tutor will say wow  you've improved  maybe she won't maybe i'll be worse i  don't know but i just thought i would  share with you that i've been having  talked about variety  that i think it's also useful to focus  at times  it can be a focus for five days it can  be a focus for two weeks  and to stay with  one  content item  but maybe vary the way you do it so  you know i'm in sentence mode sometimes  i do the you know putting the sentence  together after each sentence sometimes i  save it up to do it later on i listen to  it another thing i did was i printed  them out on paper and so i read them on  paper which is again introducing some  variety because if i read it on paper  i'm now unable to look up the word  uh rather than doing sentence by  sentence i'm now doing the whole story  so that's introducing some variety  while i remain focused on this  bit of you know content  i should add as well that  sahara is an outstanding tutor  uh she doesn't spend a lot of time  explaining the language to me she finds  me interesting content she encourages me  she has just been an unbelievable guide  to iranian culture food history  language learning content  and as i learn things of interest to me  i don't really notice the fact  that i'm learning the language although  in fact i am learning the language so  i just thought i would share that with  you my experience of the last few days  which i intend to continue until i  really feel that i've got a good grasp  on this uh particular series uh you know  and i'll leave a link to it  uh in the description box  and i mean it is part and parcel of this  whole idea of  input-based learning so i'll leave a  couple of videos as well that that touch  on related subjects because even though  what i say sometimes seems to contradict  what i said earlier in fact it's all  part of more or less the same message  which i try to present in different ways  to see if i can  stimulate people to have  more interest and more confidence  in their language learning thanks for  listening bye for now

